      "summary": "Operator confirmed the doser outlet was misaligned with the balance-enclosure hole: the powder stream largely missed the hole and piled up just behind it (issue #156). The balance saw only the fraction that fell through.",
      "detail": "Evidence: operator report + photo at https://github.com/vertical-cloud-lab/powder-doser/issues/156#issuecomment-5590508708. Signatures in this run consistent with misalignment: apparent feed ~8 mg/rev at 45 deg vs 26.3 mg/rev on the fresh 2026-08-05 fill; huge actuation counts per dose (up to 18.1 auger rev and 330 taps for <=200 mg 'delivered'); the 2026-09-08 16:46 session had flagged the low feed as suspected caking/low auger before the misalignment was discovered. Dose masses under-report actual dispensed powder by an unknown factor, so dose errors are not measurements of accuracy. Superseded by the post-re-alignment re-run.",
